Subject: Make original disc reads and asynchronous lifecycle safe on hosts

Upstream-base: 01c9a4d61904afc927d6752c3cd29fca489ff5cc

Retain the console branches and original NL API while adapting native reads to
Aurora's threaded DVD service. Keep callback state pointer-sized, reserve both
head/tail slots, reject bounds/capacity errors, and drain workers before callbacks
or pool reuse. Preserve callback entry state through reentrant operations, close
pending requests safely, and release native file state before arenas disappear.
Synchronous whole-file loading retains original allocator selection with scoped
restoration and cleanup. Custom-heap ownership and host-file loading fail
explicitly; advanced whole-file async and decompression are not in this subset.

